-- Studio MCP execute_luau, MAIN place, Edit mode only (메인 반영 runs it; the runner replaces "__MODE__").
-- Dresses the Halo Citadel (terrain: tools/worldkit/halo_terrain.luau must be applied first) with OUR OWN Tripo models from
-- ServerStorage.WorldKit3D (Halo_Gate, Halo_Cathedral, Town_Halo_Fountain3, Halo_Tower, Halo_DomeHouseA/B, Halo_Shop, Halo_Statue, Halo_ArchBridge, Halo_Stairs,
-- Halo_Balustrade, Halo_Lantern, Halo_Planter, Halo_CloudBush, Halo_Topiary, Halo_RoundTree, Halo_PotFlowers, Halo_BannerPole, Halo_Islet, Halo_FarArch).
-- Contracts kept (zone_check_halo): Bridge_Halo is NEVER touched (the only walking way out of the town); Gate_HaloTown = a Model in Map.Gates whose
-- PrimaryPart is an invisible non-colliding "Lintel" at the front edge (0, 19, -330), the split gate mesh collides (PreciseConvexDecomposition keeps the
-- arch opening free, measured 10/10); the new fountain is the kit model Town_Halo_Fountain3 (FountainFx SPECS key; Town_Halo_Fountain stays the Crossroads cloud fountain, never --replace it); nothing solid on the spawn
-- corridor (the layout planner refuses it); decor collision per kind (solid / DecorPlayerOnly / trunk post / walk-through); every prop keeps all four
-- SurfaceAppearance maps (A23-107); backdrop islets / arches (beyond the land) never collide and never answer queries.
-- Old placeholders (HaloTower, HeroStatue, HaloCastle, HaloTownTrees, Flower, ZoneSwap_halo, Town_Halo_* clones, the old gate) move to
-- ServerStorage.HaloPropsOld (attribute HaloFrom = old parent path) and come back on "restore"; nothing is destroyed.
-- Output: Map.Decor.HaloProps (Cell_x_z Models of 64 studs, ready for a client distance cull) + Map.Gates.Gate_HaloTown, rebuilt on every run.
-- MODE: "plan" = read only (kit present?, counts, triangle and part estimates); "apply" (default) = (re)build; "restore" = remove ours + put the olds back.

